{"title":"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems\">2010 AMC 12B #8</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 10B Problems\">2010 AMC 10B #17</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every high school in the city of Euclid sent a team of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students to a math contest. Each participant in the contest received a different score. Andrea's score was the median among all students, and hers was the highest score on her team. Andrea's teammates Beth and Carla placed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /><sup>th</sup> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /><sup>th</sup>, respectively. How many schools are in the city?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02fd604bd7f271ff4e8412e5d292d68770452dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 22 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 23 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> schools. This means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> people. Because no one's score was the same as another person's score, that means that there could only have been <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> median score. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an odd number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, because there wouldn't be a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />th place if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> was. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> either, because that would tie Andrea and Beth or Andrea's place would be worse than Beth's. Thus, the only possible answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b7c4f7903627066c8002c1bfb6fb0a61829fb4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{(B)}\\ 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be Andrea's place. We know that she was the highest on her team, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349c70db7121b7a4bc7552a22ced7c9acbe7de17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the median, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6873715a60ff7706da71b8cad30cead78b1ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> to the left and right of the median, so the total number of people is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f1daa9ab402c89fd76285ac43ae812ff2e5b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and the number of schools is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab3441858e47560ccd3b12300af80d1b8d15e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2a-1)/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b20df674018637c43520d7f5789f4a020d90a670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a-1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\implies a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"318\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f1daa9ab402c89fd76285ac43ae812ff2e5b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> is the rank of the last-place person, and one of Andrea's teammates already got 64th place, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/b/50b53d56cd2af918734408a5b4aa59edc4dd1d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a-1 &gt; 64 \\implies a \\ge 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Putting it all together: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b7e700aafcd657916d8bd617cdd4d1b60bc6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33 \\le a &lt; 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc95d74d277f19e2896fd4ad9cbeb11dad43830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, so clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b7bf59e10f7d19db6e57fb7df7dbb6ea711eb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 35$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, and the number of schools as we got before is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d60113555a0b950cc3313b8ec1fbf784761957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2a-1)/3 = 69/3 = \\boxed{\\mathbf{(B)}\\ 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"233\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~adihaya\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since all students have distinct scores, we can assume the scores are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the total number of students. From Solution 1, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is odd.\n</p><p>Andrea’s score is the median, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe17b72c8b0c87f70b8ca803e54a1e5a4547af63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{S+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"39\" />.\nBeth and Carla have scores\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b66e05bc474cba73e70cf19cacf4a24a5e750f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = S - 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e67b54fc77868cdd1a8b1ccf41691415434fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\quad C = S - 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />.\nSince Andrea has the highest score among her teammates, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de52e5c3f75e3091110b9926a28b8da02f23af7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A &gt; B \\quad \\text{and} \\quad A &gt; C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />.\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441f711bfbe4ebd68eddc9360cb3ebca4480c94e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S+1}{2} &gt; S - 37 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{S+1}{2} &gt; S - 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"310\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Solving these inequalities:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/455c7f042a1c555fa570f0e8b911a77d38719716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S+1}{2} &gt; S - 37 \\Rightarrow S &lt; 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"209\" height=\"39\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0f1a434f039f27e5ab8cf04e4a6ebdea8c3713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S+1}{2} &gt; S - 64 \\Rightarrow S &lt; 129$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"218\" height=\"39\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/7457fc1626fe866dfcbe0db9ecefc833717b6090.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &lt; 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />.\nWe also have&#160;: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/6998a7cd95c55af78e87aef18e47b161ac5d9a93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B + C &gt; A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />.\nSubstituting:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c09bafbe19a95668a4d6535cb3a9855430660f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(S - 37) + (S - 64) &gt; \\frac{S+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"229\" height=\"39\" />.\nThis simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bf13d9b07e6e359de1823b8532e23e4ac230111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2S - 101 &gt; \\frac{S+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1fdd00ea4e1888a7b7835bb9929facc7f2d3028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 4S - 202 &gt; S + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1e017a60dcc1a7fac591d531ebd101ec840e8e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 3S &gt; 203$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/7521ec23e58bb187886fae0a900ad179bd6cf14a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow S &gt; \\frac{203}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Since students are grouped into teams of 3, let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47de8c2404a0568b7cec846a76527dee8bf429be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 3t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />.\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1db104bc5ea9165fe80432f4356030ec783b944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{203}{3} &lt; S &lt; 75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8d2de14a69b56bd5b59feae989b4cbe5a81311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow 22 &lt; t &lt; 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />\nBecause t has to be an odd number in this range we get&#160;:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db44755925fefe4079e5782438ebbbf0bae9273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1a712adc043b2b77538eee38e0a5f9295996de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{(B)\\ 23}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"69\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~Gamor\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FQO-0E2zUVI?t=297\">https://youtu.be/FQO-0E2zUVI?t=297</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit 